  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"1303\" data-end=\"1327\"><strong data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1325\">Normal Response:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1427\">\n<li data-start=\"1328\" data-end=\"1386\">\n<p data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1386\">Decrement <strong data-start=\"1340\" data-end=\"1349\">&lt; 10%</strong> between 1st and 4th/5th responses.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1427\">\n<p data-start=\"1389\" data-end=\"1427\">No significant change post-exercise.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1484\"><strong data-start=\"1431\" data-end=\"1482\">Abnormal Response (Suggestive of NMJ Disorder):</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1696\">\n<li data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1547\">\n<p data-start=\"1487\" data-end=\"1547\">Decrement <strong data-start=\"1497\" data-end=\"1506\">&gt; 10%</strong> in low-frequency stimulation (2&ndash;3 Hz).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1623\">\n<p data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1623\"><strong data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1563\">Increment</strong> after exercise (seen in presynaptic disorders like LEMS).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1624\" data-end=\"1696\">\n<p data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1696\"><strong data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1650\">Persistent decrement</strong> after exercise (seen in Myasthenia Gravis).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
